# sqladmin admin panel

Runtime: sqladmin (`uv add sqladmin[auth]`). Install only with the database bundle
(`python-sqlalchemy` + `python-db-sessions`).

Views live in `project/infrastructure/apps/admin.py` and are mounted from
`project/infrastructure/apps/api.py`. Reuse the async engine from
`aengine_factory()` (`python-db-sessions`); sqladmin opens its own sessions. Admin is the
one presentation-side module allowed to import ORM models: it never goes through
repositories or use cases, and domain code never imports the admin module.

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI
from sqladmin import Admin, ModelView

from project.components.orders.models import Order
from project.components.users.models import User
from project.infrastructure.adapters.database import aengine_factory


class UserAdmin(ModelView, model=User):
    name_plural = "Users"
    category = "Accounts"
    column_list = [User.id, User.email, User.created_at]
    column_details_list = [User.id, User.email, User.created_at]
    form_excluded_columns = [User.password_hash]


def mount_admin(app: FastAPI) -> None:
    admin = Admin(
        app,
        aengine_factory(),
        authentication_backend=AdminAuth(secret_key=Settings().SECRET_KEY),
    )
    admin.add_view(UserAdmin)
    admin.add_view(ModelView(Order))
```

Set `column_list` and form columns explicitly on every view: the defaults expose every
model column in the list and make every column editable. Exclude secrets and server-side
columns (`password_hash`, `created_at`) from forms.

## Authentication

Always authenticate the panel (`sqladmin[auth]`). Subclass
`sqladmin.authentication.AuthenticationBackend` (`login` / `logout` / `authenticate`) and add
`SessionMiddleware` with the same `secret_key` as the backend. Operator credentials come
from Settings (`ADMIN_USER` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD`), never from code.

```python
import secrets

from sqladmin.authentication import AuthenticationBackend
from starlette.middleware.sessions import SessionMiddleware
from starlette.requests import Request

from project.settings import Settings


class AdminAuth(AuthenticationBackend):
    async def login(self, request: Request) -> bool:
        form = await request.form()
        granted = secrets.compare_digest(str(form["username"]), Settings().ADMIN_USER) and (
            secrets.compare_digest(str(form["password"]), Settings().ADMIN_PASSWORD)
        )
        if granted:
            request.session.update({"admin": True})
        return granted

    async def logout(self, request: Request) -> bool:
        request.session.clear()
        return True

    async def authenticate(self, request: Request) -> bool:
        return bool(request.session.get("admin"))


app.add_middleware(SessionMiddleware, secret_key=Settings().SECRET_KEY)
```

Merge `SECRET_KEY`, `ADMIN_USER`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD` into `settings.py`
(`python-architecture/python-settings.mdc`).

## layers.toml

```toml
[layers.admin]
description = "Admin panel over ORM models; the only presentation-side module importing models"
contains_modules = [
    "project.infrastructure.apps.admin",
    "project.infrastructure.apps.admin.*",
]
depends_on = ["libs", "adapters", "repositories"]

[libs.sqladmin]
allowed_in = ["admin"]
```

Add `"admin"` to `[layers.presentation]` `depends_on`. Add `"admin"` to
`[libs.sqlalchemy]` `allowed_in` only when the admin module imports `sqlalchemy` directly.

## Tests

Cover the panel in e2e (`python-tests`): login rejects wrong credentials, list and detail
render for an authenticated operator. Do not unit-test sqladmin itself.
